From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Bruce Jones <jason@brucejones.biz>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: romulus15: add the QSPI touchpad

The Surface Laptop 7 15" touchpad is a HID-over-SPI device on spi19, on
four data lanes. Its tree has no node for it, so the laptop has no
touchpad under Linux. The drivers are already here: spi-hid and the QSPI
mode of spi-geni-qcom came in with the Surface Pro 11 patches.

Describe the bus and the touchpad. The wiring follows the 15" support in
github.com/ItsLucas/surface-laptop-7-ubuntu-kernel, which took it from
github.com/ProgrammerIn-wonderland/ELLX-Kernel, rewritten for the
hid-over-spi binding. The report addresses and opcodes are the same as
the Surface Pro 11 digitizer's.

The pad comes up in a mouse mode: pointer, tap, press to click. It stays
there even with Input Mode set to 3, and report 0x81 never arrives.
iptsd gives multi-finger input.

Tested on the Surface Laptop 7 15": the node boots, enumerates as
045E:0C77 with no SPI bus errors, and the pad works across a lid close
and a suspend and resume.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jason Bruce Jones <jason@brucejones.biz>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts | 91 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 91 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts
index 4751ad9..b808cf4 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts
@@ -5,9 +5,100 @@
 
 /dts-v1/;
 
+#include <dt-bindings/dma/qcom-gpi.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/irq.h>
+
 #include "x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi"
 
 / {
 	model = "Microsoft Surface Laptop 7 (15 inch)";
 	compatible = "microsoft,romulus15", "qcom,x1e80100";
+
+	vreg_ts_5p0: regulator-ts-5p0 {
+		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
+
+		regulator-name = "vreg_ts_5p0";
+		regulator-min-microvolt = <5000000>;
+		regulator-max-microvolt = <5000000>;
+
+		gpio = <&tlmm 65 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		enable-active-high;
+
+		regulator-boot-on;
+		startup-delay-us = <500000>;
+	};
+};
+
+&gpi_dma2 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&spi19 {
+	compatible = "qcom,geni-qspi";
+	dmas = <&gpi_dma2 0 3 QCOM_GPI_QSPI>,
+	       <&gpi_dma2 1 3 QCOM_GPI_QSPI>;
+	dma-names = "tx", "rx";
+	pinctrl-0 = <&qup_qspi19_data_clk>, <&qup_qspi19_cs>,
+		    <&qup_qspi19_data23>;
+	pinctrl-names = "default";
+	status = "okay";
+
+	touchpad@0 {
+		compatible = "hid-over-spi";
+		reg = <0>;
+		spi-max-frequency = <20000000>;
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 3 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+		reset-gpios = <&tlmm 120 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+		vdd-supply = <&vreg_ts_5p0>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&touchpad_int>, <&touchpad_reset>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		input-report-header-address = <0x1000>;
+		input-report-body-address = <0x1004>;
+		output-report-address = <0x2000>;
+		read-opcode = /bits/ 8 <0xeb>;
+		write-opcode = /bits/ 8 <0xe2>;
+		hid-over-spi-flags = <0xa000>;
+	};
+};
+
+&tlmm {
+	qup_qspi19_cs: qup-qspi19-cs-state {
+		pins = "gpio79";
+		function = "qup2_se3";
+		drive-strength = <6>;
+		bias-pull-down;
+	};
+
+	qup_qspi19_data_clk: qup-qspi19-data-clk-state {
+		/* IO0, IO1, CLK */
+		pins = "gpio76", "gpio77", "gpio78";
+		function = "qup2_se3";
+		drive-strength = <6>;
+		bias-pull-down;
+	};
+
+	qup_qspi19_data23: qup-qspi19-data23-state {
+		/* IO2, IO3 */
+		pins = "gpio66", "gpio67";
+		function = "qup2_se3";
+		drive-strength = <6>;
+		bias-pull-down;
+	};
+
+	touchpad_int: touchpad-int-state {
+		pins = "gpio3";
+		function = "gpio";
+		input-enable;
+		bias-pull-up;
+	};
+
+	touchpad_reset: touchpad-reset-state {
+		pins = "gpio120";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <16>;
+		bias-disable;
+	};
 };
